Overlay patch 0031: visionOS platform dispatch (VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK
Phase 01; = sibling ports' visionos-dispatch).

The leetal toolchain sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=visionOS for
PLATFORM=SIMULATOR_VISIONOS/VISIONOS, but the whole tree (upstream + our iOS
overlay CMake) dispatches on STREQUAL "iOS" at 16+ sites. Rather than patch
every site, flip CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME back to "iOS" right after project(): by
then compilers, sysroot, and Xcode's SDKROOT are locked, so the flip only
affects dispatch conditionals. Real visionOS-ness continues from the SDK
(TARGET_OS_VISION=1). SOH_VISIONOS stays a cache var for genuinely vision-
specific deltas (Swift entry lib, plist — patch 0012). Three flips because
each project()/toolchain include re-runs platform init: top level, LUS's
project(), and after LUS's ios-toolchain-populate include. No-op for iOS
(condition never true).

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,6 +2,16 @@
 
 # Set the project version and language
 project(Starship VERSION 2.0.0 LANGUAGES C CXX ASM)
+
+# SOH_IOS (overlay 0031): visionOS builds (PLATFORM=SIMULATOR_VISIONOS /
+# VISIONOS) dispatch as iOS throughout the tree. Compilers and SDK are already
+# fixed by the toolchain here; only the STREQUAL "iOS" conditionals care.
+# TARGET_OS_VISION (from the xros SDK) remains the source-level discriminator.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+    set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+    set(IOS 1)
+    set(SOH_VISIONOS 1)
+endif()
 include(FetchContent)
 
 set(NATO_PHONETIC_ALPHABET
--- a/libultraship/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libultraship/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -10,6 +10,16 @@
 
 project(libultraship LANGUAGES C CXX)
 
+# SOH_IOS (overlay 0031): visionOS builds (PLATFORM=SIMULATOR_VISIONOS /
+# VISIONOS) dispatch as iOS throughout the tree. Compilers and SDK are already
+# fixed by the toolchain here; only the STREQUAL "iOS" conditionals care.
+# TARGET_OS_VISION (from the xros SDK) remains the source-level discriminator.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+    set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+    set(IOS 1)
+    set(SOH_VISIONOS 1)
+endif()
+
 if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Darwin" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
     enable_language(OBJCXX)
     set(CMAKE_OBJC_FLAGS "${CMAKE_OBJC_FLAGS} -fobjc-arc")
@@ -57,6 +67,14 @@
 # === Platform Specific Configuration ===
 if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "iOS")
     include(cmake/ios-toolchain-populate.cmake)
+    # SOH_IOS (overlay 0031): the toolchain include re-ran leetal's platform
+    # init IN THIS SCOPE, resetting CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME to visionOS again —
+    # re-flip so src/ (compile defs, __IOS__) dispatches as iOS.
+    if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+        set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+        set(IOS 1)
+        set(SOH_VISIONOS 1)
+    endif()
 endif()
 
